00:13:13.209 --> 00:13:18.399
about, for example, merging in a rotary or
traffic circle, whether it's the right time

00:13:18.399 --> 00:13:24.500
or it's not the right time or about getting
through a yellow light or not, this is something

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:26.790
that it's really been reduced to.

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:30.389
It's happening in a very, very small amount
of time.

00:13:30.389 --> 00:13:34.800
And we're sort of intuitively considering
the position of pedestrians and how far we

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:36.399
are from the light.

00:13:36.399 --> 00:13:42.060
In some of these cases, there will be variability,
but it seems that that it's actually quite

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:48.510
hard to replicate it accurately with an artificial
intelligence or with computers.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:53.610
What about those cases where noise seems to
be a sort of uniquely human ability to make

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:56.449
these judgment calls in a very small amount
of time?

00:13:56.449 --> 00:13:59.360
Speaker 5: So we wouldn't call this noise.

